            <div class="lead" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:32px;color:#bbb;">
              Social media management for small businesses costs <strong>USD 500-3,500/month in 2026</strong> depending on platforms, post frequency, and whether ads are included. Below are the actual pricing tiers, what gets delivered at each tier, and how to spot agencies that are overcharging for thin output.
            </div>
            <style>article a {color:rgb(20,120,190);text-decoration:underline;} article h2 {margin-top:48px;} article h3 {margin-top:32px;}</style>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Three pricing tiers most agencies offer</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-3">Tier 1 — Starter (USD 500-1,200 / month)</h3>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:16px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">1-2 platforms (typically Instagram + Facebook)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">12-20 posts/month (4-5 per week)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Stock photography or basic AI-generated graphics</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Basic monthly report (likes, follows, reach)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Comment moderation: limited or none</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Suitable for: solo founders, very local businesses, very small budgets</li></ul>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-3">Tier 2 — Growth (USD 1,200-2,500 / month)</h3>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:16px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">2-3 platforms (Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn or TikTok)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">20-40 posts/month with custom graphics</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Stories and Reels production (4-8/month)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Hashtag research and caption writing by experienced strategist</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Monthly content calendar approval</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Comment moderation included</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Suitable for: growing small businesses, e-commerce brands, professional services</li></ul>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-3">Tier 3 — Premium (USD 2,500-5,000+ / month)</h3>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:16px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">3-4 platforms</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">30-60+ posts/month with original photography or video</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Reels / TikTok production with custom video editing</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Influencer outreach and partnership management</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Community management (DMs, comments, reviews)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Detailed analytics with strategy adjustments</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Includes paid social ads management (10-15% of ad spend)</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;">Suitable for: established brands with USD 1M+ revenue</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What drives price differences</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Custom photography / video:</strong> add USD 500-2,000/month for in-house production</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Multi-language posts:</strong> add 30-50% per additional language</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Daily posting cadence:</strong> typically 2x the cost of weekly cadence</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Paid ads management on top:</strong> 10-15% of ad spend, or USD 500-1,500/month flat</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Influencer management:</strong> add USD 800-2,000/month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Brand strategy / quarterly planning:</strong> some agencies bundle this; others charge separately</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Pakistan-specific pricing (2026)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Starter:</strong> PKR 30K-60K / month (USD 110-215)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Growth:</strong> PKR 60K-150K / month (USD 215-540)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Premium:</strong> PKR 150K-400K / month (USD 540-1,430)</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What to demand before signing a retainer</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Sample content calendar</strong> — 1 week's worth as a deliverable preview</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Named strategist</strong> who owns your account (not just an agency name)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Monthly KPIs in writing</strong> — what they're optimizing toward</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>30-day exit clause</strong> for the first 90 days</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Access to your accounts</strong> — never let an agency 'own' your social media accounts</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Red flags</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>'Guaranteed growth' promises</strong> — no agency can guarantee specific follower or engagement numbers ethically</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Buying followers / engagement</strong> — kills your reach algorithmically; never worth it</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Identical content across multiple clients</strong> — sign of template-based churn-and-burn agency</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>No real photographer / videographer access</strong> — you'll end up with stock-photo soup</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>'Performance-based' pricing</strong> — usually means they take payment for engagement metrics rather than business outcomes</li></ul>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4 mt-5">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How many posts per month is right?</h3><p>Quality > quantity. 15-25 great posts beat 50 mediocre ones. Most platforms reward consistent posting (3-5x/week), not high volume.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Do I need to be on TikTok?</h3><p>Only if your audience is there. TikTok works for B2C consumer brands and lifestyle products. For B2B services, real estate, healthcare, professional services — usually skip TikTok and double down on LinkedIn or Instagram.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can I do social media in-house?</h3><p>Yes, especially with AI tools (ChatGPT for captions, Canva for graphics). The trade-off: founder time. Most founders find their time is worth more than the USD 500-1,500/month they'd save.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How do I measure social media ROI?</h3><p>Track: (1) direct traffic to your site from social, (2) qualified leads attributed to social via UTM tracking, (3) brand-search lift over time (people Googling your brand name). Pure 'engagement' metrics (likes, follows) are vanity unless they correlate to one of the three above.</p>
